        </townGoods>
        <ariseAges>0~3</ariseAges>
      </li>
    </modExtensions>
  </FactionDef>

  <!-- ===================== Their people ===================== -->

  <!--
    How alike they look (docs/design/peoples.md, "Release E"): the order's coat, not its cut. Every reader wears a coat of
    any cut in storm slate (the game's dusters, jackets and parkas; Vanilla Apparel Expanded's coats), hung with
    brass-capped vials; under it whatever they like (the game's and Vanilla Apparel Expanded's clothes, hats and caps;
    Vanilla Apparel Expanded - Accessories' packs and tool belts, never the soldiers' belts). The storm-walkers who see
    the readers through the storms share one kit: the slate duster over a flak vest, a helmet and the game's rifles; in
    the tribal and medieval ages crossbows (Vanilla Weapons Expanded, Medieval 2's arbalest), in the spacer age charge
    rifles. The first reader may wear Royalty's psychic finery. Most of the readers are psycasters (Royalty's psylink;
    with Vanilla Psycasts Expanded a Staticlord's or a Frostshaper's path), a few A RimWorld of Magic's storm-born or
    frost-hearted. They carry herbs for the cold, a book of the storms or warm cloth. Without any mod: the game's coats
    and clothes, revolvers, rifles and knives.
  -->
  <PawnKindDef Name="Rimfolk_StormglassKindBase" Abstract="True">
    <race>Human</race>
    <defaultFactionDef>Rimfolk_Stormglass</defaultFactionDef>
    <chemicalAddictionChance>0.02</chemicalAddictionChance>
    <backstoryCryptosleepCommonality>0.02</backstoryCryptosleepCommonality>
    <invNutrition>2.55</invNutrition>
    <specificApparelRequirements>
      <!-- Storm slate on the duster and the jacket, whoever wears one. -->
      <li><apparelDef>Apparel_Duster</apparelDef><color>(0.28, 0.34, 0.50)</color></li>
      <li><apparelDef>Apparel_Jacket</apparelDef><color>(0.28, 0.34, 0.50)</color></li>
    </specificApparelRequirements>
  </PawnKindDef>

